 ## Overview
-Deferred Voxel Shading is a real-time global illumination technique that merges voxel cone tracing with deferred shading to compute indirect lighting effects such as diffuse/specular reflection, color blending, emissive materials, and ambient occlusion [S2, unofficial]. Unlike forward rendering approaches, it delays lighting computations until the fragment shader stage, avoiding redundant calculations for overlapping geometry and enabling efficient handling of complex lighting scenarios with multiple light sources [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Voxel Cone Tracing](1454-voxel-cone-tracing.md) by introducing anisotropic voxel representations and deferred direct illumination integration.
+Deferred Voxel Shading is a four-step real-time global illumination technique that merges voxel cone tracing with deferred shading to compute indirect lighting effects, including diffuse/specular reflection, color blending, emissive materials, indirect shadows, and ambient occlusion [S2, unofficial]. Unlike forward rendering approaches, it delays lighting computations until the fragment shader stage, avoiding redundant calculations for overlapping polygons and enhancing performance in scenes with many light sources [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Voxel Cone Tracing](1454-voxel-cone-tracing.md) by introducing anisotropic voxel filtering and deferred integration of direct and indirect light.
 
